    <bpmn:process id="W_W5562" name="W5562. Vehicle-Impact &amp; Storefront-Crash Response Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: A motor vehicle strikes a BuildRight building — a storefront or entrance impact, a parking-lot collision with the building face or support columns, a loading-dock/delivery-vehicle impact, or a boom/crane crash against the structure while customers or staff are on site
Frequency: Rare but chain-real event class: ~2–4 vehicle-into-building strikes per year across ~205 roadside sites with parking lots and dock aprons (big-box formats sit behind driving surfaces); most are low-speed parking-lot contacts, the tail case is a high-speed storefront intrusion during trading
Volume: 1 event × 1 site × the crash-surface scope (glazing, canopy, columns, racking near the impact line) × the trading-impact tier (partial-zone closure to full closure); each event also opens the driver/third-party liability track and the structural-clearance gate
Owner: Store Manager (site command); Head of Customer Safety (protocol &amp; reopen gate)
Participants: Regional Manager, Security Guard / Loss Prevention, Facilities &amp; Maintenance (W650 call-out), Structural Engineer (retainer), PNP traffic investigator, third-party insurer (driver&#x27;s liability desk), VS-26 (property/BI claim, W876), VS-147.3 (injury/claims chain where injuries occur), Store Communications (VS-63), Legal (VS-100 demand &amp; subrogation posture)
Source: workflow W5562 — Vehicle-Impact &amp; Storefront-Crash Response Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5562_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5562_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5562_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5562_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5562_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5562_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5562_Lane2" name="Facilities">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5562_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5562_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5562_Lane3" name="Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5562_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5562_Lane4" name="Insurance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5562_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5562_Lane5" name="Head of Customer Safety">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5562_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5562_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5562_Start7" name="A motor vehicle strikes a BuildRight building — a storefront or entrance impact, a…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5562_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5562_Task8" name="Crash-scene safety &amp; command">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Crash-scene safety &amp; command: hold-back cordon (vehicle instability, fuel leak, glass); isolate power/fuel at the meter where the impact struck utilities; first aid per W501 with injuries routed via W140/VS-147.3; request PNP traffic investigation
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Security Guard
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5562_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5562_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5562_Task9" name="Evidence preservation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Evidence preservation: CCTV preservation hold (W838); scene photos before any cleanup; witness details; driver/vehicle/insurer details on the incident record; no fault statements by anyone
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5562_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5562_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5562_Task10" name="Structural triage">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Structural triage: Facilities + structural-engineer call-out assess the impact zone — glazing, canopy, columns, the racking line behind the face; red-tag zones cordoned; occupancy of unaffected zones documented
Responsible (R): Facilities / Structural Engineer
Accountable (A): Head of Customer Safety
Duration: 2–6 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5562_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5562_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5562_Task11" name="Liability posture">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Liability posture: the driver&#x27;s CTPL and own-damage insurance is the primary claim track; BuildRight&#x27;s property loss runs as subrogation; Legal issues the demand/notice letter to driver, owner and insurer
Responsible (R): Legal / Insurance
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 1–2 days elapsed</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5562_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5562_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5562_Task12" name="Claim initiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Claim initiation: property-claim pack (photos, engineer&#x27;s report, repair quotes) to the third-party insurer; own-policy engagement (VS-26 W876) for the uninsured gap and business interruption
Responsible (R): Insurance / VS-26 Claims
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–5 days elapsed</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5562_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5562_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5562_Task13" name="Trading-continuity decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Trading-continuity decision: partial trade behind the cordon is the default; full closure rides the Regional Manager closure authority (the E-02 custody — W2510 decides, W850 executes) when the impact zone touches exits, utilities or occupied selling space; documented either way
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Regional Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: On assessment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5562_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5562_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5562_Task14" name="Repair &amp; reopen gate">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Repair &amp; reopen gate: repairs under permit where structure is touched; no reopen of red-tagged zones until the structural engineer&#x27;s written clearance and — where load-bearing elements were struck — the LGU building official&#x27;s clearance (the W5537 BFP-gate analog)
Responsible (R): Facilities / Head of Customer Safety
Accountable (A): Head of Customer Safety
Duration: Per repair scope</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5562_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5562_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5562_Task15" name="After-action &amp; retrofit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: After-action &amp; retrofit: the incident feeds the site-standards register — bollard/barrier adequacy at the struck face reviewed per this PA and VS-138 PM; claims outcome reconciles to the safety-investment backlog
Responsible (R): Head of Customer Safety / Facilities
Accountable (A): Head of Customer Safety
Duration: 1–2 weeks post-event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5562_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5562_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5562_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5562_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5562_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-672 (ensure controlled execution — In-Store Customer Safety Operations &amp; Hazard Control (PA-147.2).) | - operational: crash-scene cordons and no-statement rules briefed at every store; red-tag/reopen decisions documented with the engineer&#x27;s written clearance; subrogation files reconciled to claim outcomes
Owner: Store Manager (site command); Head of Customer Safety (protocol &amp; reopen gate)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5562_Assoc18" sourceRef="W5562_Annotation17" targetRef="W5562_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
